stages.prompt:
## CONTEXT RESET
Plan {{story_title}} for {{project_name}} at {{source_url}}. Read-only analysis only; no repository mutation or coding.
Readiness: {{readiness_artifact}}
Slice context: {{context_md}}
Tasks: {{tasks}}
Decisions: {{adrs}}
Related code: {{related_files}}
Propose a bounded plan: existing code to reuse, files to change, state owners and consumers, preserved contracts, named tests at the relevant boundary, dependencies, rollout and rollback. Link each consequential decision to affected code and a verification step. Distinguish mocked tests from persisted-data/consumer checks. STOP on missing or conflicting requirements. Submit the plan and evidence for human approval; do not resolve architectural ambiguity by guessing.

Review {{story_title}}.
Readiness: {{readiness_artifact}}
Plan: {{plan_artifact}}
The host runner must authenticate and authorize the reviewer, reread current evidence, recompute the score/fingerprint and show the exact plan being approved. Accept only an explicit approve, bounce or escalate decision with rationale. Record reviewer identity, decision, time, evidence fingerprint, rubric version and plan hash in a trusted audit store. Reject stale, missing, non-coding-band or specification-only evidence. Record named checkpoints for AI Assisted work. If evidence or plan changed, bounce to readiness; never advance on missing input. These requirements must be implemented by the host runner; this template alone cannot enforce them.

## CONTEXT RESET
Implement {{story_title}} for {{project_name}} at {{source_url}} only after the host verifies the approval.
Approval: {{approval_artifact}}
Readiness: {{readiness_artifact}}
Plan: {{plan_artifact}}
Read {{context_md_path}} and referenced decisions. Work within {{slice_directory}}. Follow the repository's stack and commands, reuse canonical owners/models, and verify contracts with the approved tests. Use parameterized queries where applicable; do not add real secrets or private data to examples. STOP and ask on missing/changed evidence, ambiguous behavior, failed authorization or changed plan; return to readiness for fresh approval before another coding attempt. Report actual test commands/results, including failures or checks not run. Open a draft pull request against {{target_branch}} on an authorized {{work_item_key}}-short-description branch. Never auto-merge. Keep the draft linked to the approved evidence; an agent must not authorize itself.

Draft PR: {{pr_url}}
Branch: {{branch_name}}
Implementation and verification report: {{execute_artifact}}
Report only verified results. Leave merge and release decisions to authorized humans.
